Here is a complete drop-in version that validates both locations before hashing, records the external volume label, and exits with a distinct failure code when a folder or drive is unavailable:

```powershell
$PcRoot       = "C:\Users\YourName\ReferenceFiles"
$ExternalRoot = "E:\ReferenceFiles"
$ReportRoot   = "C:\BackupReports"

