The API’s `GET /download/form` should only set a CSRF cookie and return an ordinary HTML form whose `POST /download/exchange` contains the intent and CSRF value; the POST authenticates the user from SSO, atomically consumes `download:intent:{intent}` with `GETDEL` or the Lua fallback, verifies `payload["sub"]`, and streams the CSV directly—so no download code is placed in the exchange URL or cookie. If even the intent must not appear in browser history or logs, the only robust alternative is a small same-origin browser page that receives it through `sessionStorage` or a server-side user session; an iframe-based Streamlit component should not be used for this flow.

