Yes—use `LockService` to prevent overlapping runs, then re-read each candidate’s payment-status cell immediately before sending; this reduces the chance of emailing someone whose payment was just recorded (though no spreadsheet script can make that check perfectly atomic with an incoming transfer). Wrap each send in `try/catch` and record failures in a **Reminder errors** sheet:

```javascript
function sendPendingReminders() {
  const lock = LockService.getScriptLock();
  lock.tryLock(30000);
  try {
    const ss = SpreadsheetApp.getActive();
    const sheet = ss.getSheetByName("RSVP responses");
    const data = sheet.getDataRange().getValues(), headers = data.shift();
    const c = name => headers.indexOf(name);
    const emailCol = c("Email"), statusCol = c("Payment status");
    const sentCol = c("Reminder sent"), nameCol = c("Name");
    const errors = ss.getSheetByName("Reminder errors") ||
      ss.insertSheet("Reminder errors");

    data.forEach((row, i) => {
      if (String(row[statusCol]).toLowerCase() !== "pending" ||
          row[sentCol] || !row[emailCol]) return;

      SpreadsheetApp.flush();
      const currentStatus = String(sheet.getRange(i + 2, statusCol + 1).getValue()).toLowerCase();
      if (currentStatus !== "pending") return;

      try {
        GmailApp.sendEmail(row[emailCol], "Reminder: Shop Night payment",
          `Hi ${row[nameCol]},\n\nOur records show your materials contribution is still pending. Please send it by e-transfer to [email], or reply if you need another option.\n\nThanks!`);
        sheet.getRange(i + 2, sentCol + 1).setValue(new Date());
      } catch (err) {
        errors.appendRow([new Date(), row[nameCol], row[emailCol], err.message]);
      }
    });
  } finally {
    lock.releaseLock();
  }
}
```

If a send succeeds but the “Reminder sent” update fails, check Gmail’s sent mail before retrying to avoid a duplicate; for a one-time trigger, also keep the error log for manual follow-up.

